<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14053" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dĭœcēsis</span></b> ,
		is, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διοίκησις</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A governor's jurisdiction, a district</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 3,
				8, 4</span></i> (<i><span class="en">ib. 13, 53</span></i> and 67,
			written as Greek); <i><span class="en">Cod. Theod. 7, 6,
			3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Amm. 17, 7, 6</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In eccl. Lat., <i>a bishop's jurisdiction, a diocese</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 7, 6 <i>med.</i></span></i>; sometimes also <i>a parish</i>,
					<i><span class="en">id. ib. 9, 16</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
